# Reindex Realm

## Summary
Host command — reindex a realm using the lighter/default mode. This republishes a from-scratch indexing job but only revisits files whose indexed state appears stale based on current mtime, deletion, or error semantics. Use this when a user wants to pick up normal recent changes or refresh a realm without performing a full reindex.. Available to
cards and commands via the runtime loader, and to AI assistant rooms as a
tool.

## Example
```ts
import ReindexRealmTool from '@cardstack/boxel-host/commands/reindex-realm';

let result = await new ReindexRealmTool(commandContext).execute({
  /* input fields */
} as any);
```
`commandContext` comes from `@context.commandContext` inside any card
format. In an AI room the same tool is invoked by name (action verb: Reindex).
